msgstr "A period is written in DATES while the outage log is written in UTC moments, so midnight of the period has to be midnight somewhere definite. Declared on the contract itself rather than taken from whoever is logged in: if the same period measured by two people in two time zones gives two figures, no certificate stands up. A user who has declared no time zone makes Odoo treat everything as UTC — seven hours out, and those seven hours shift downtime into the neighbouring period exactly at the contract-year boundary."

